{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1480164-multi-splat-when-do-you-ignore-breaking-points-for-killing-non-humans","id":1480164,"title":"Multi-Splat: When do you ignore Breaking Points for killing non-humans?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-05-05T08:29:11-07:00","id":1480164,"title":"Multi-Splat: When do you ignore Breaking Points for killing non-humans?","content":"I'm working on codifying some rules for Breaking Points in my mixed splat game. I've got every splat represented including Beast.<br /> <br /> Raw:<ul><li>Mortal/Hunters = Integrity</li> <li>Vampires = Humanity</li> <li>Werewolf = Harmony (Fine with killing Spirits, not a breaking point towards flesh RAW as far as I can tell)</li> <li>Mage = Wisdom</li> <li>Promethean = Torment (?) (Not a stat, but I'd say murder is probably a Torment Trigger though not RAW as far as I can tell)</li> <li>Geist/Sin-Eater = Crisis Point (?) (Not sure, Sin-Eaters seem very unphased to killing people unless its similar to their own or their Geist's death)</li> <li>Mummy = Memory (?) (Probably not)</li> <li>Demon = Cover (Only if killing people is not part of their Cover)</li> <li>Beast = Satiety (Killing people actually helps this)</li> <li>Deviant = Stability (?) (Talks about how Instability risks harming innocent people so seems like a contender)</li> </ul>Most of these have rules constituting Breaking Points for harming people. I think Beast and Mummy are pretty immune to killing things as far as Breaking Points go, but the others I'm not sure.<br /> <br /> Now what if I extend this to sentient beings? Do Slashers count? Do Ghosts/Spirits/Angels/Other Ephemerals count (if permanent killing, i.e. drain essence and corpus)?<br /> <br /> What do you all think? <br /> Killing by Accident or in Self-Defense is already a -4 Breaking Point for Integrity.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25291-donteatrawhagis","user":"DontEatRawHagis","date":". 05-05-2022, 11:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25291-donteatrawhagis","name":"DontEatRawHagis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"211"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-05T09:14:08-07:00","id":1480168,"title":"","content":"Deviants don't suffer breaking points. They risk Faltering if they act contrary to a Touchstone, but their Loyalty and Conviction won't be threatened for killing someone who isn't a Touchstone. In general, though, I think that if the person doing the killing can recognize their victim as a person, even if they are not a human, and they suffer Breaking Points for killing humans, they should suffer a Breaking Point for killing the person. If you see a spirit of murder that looks like a giant floating hand gripping the hair of a hundred severed heads you are probably just going to think that is &quot;a monster&quot; unless you have knowledge of spirits; if the ghost of a businessman is begging for his unlife while you brandish his bane, a Rolex wristwatch, that's going to be different.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12738-minty","name":"Minty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"222"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-05T09:33:02-07:00","id":1480175,"title":"","content":"If you've seen that it can understand language and communicate, it's a breaking point in terms of psychic shock for killing a person.<br /> <br /> Some supernaturals don't really have a system for suffering &quot;psychic shocks&quot; of this type: werewolves, bound, demons, beasts, and deviants. Werewolves' Harmony is moved by murder, but Harmony breaking points aren't really traumatic or debilitating in nature. Bound <i>geists</i> suffer crisis points but murder is not a crisis point by default. Beasts and deviants, if anything, derive psychic benefits from murder. Demons are the closest match that isn't a direct psychic shock, as while a demonic compromise has nothing to do with the demon's feelings or psychology, an action that would be an Integrity breaking point for that Cover if the Cover were (still?) human is a good guideline for actions that risk compromise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":522,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","user":"Stupid Loserman","date":". 05-05-2022, 12:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-05T12:39:28-07:00","id":1480196,"title":"","content":"Beast doesn't have breaking points... but that doesn't mean killing people is all positives. It's important to remember that Beasts can overfeed to fairly drastic consequences (so killing people to get more out of feeding is adding risk): specifically turning off all your supernatural powers that would let you deal with the consequences of killing people. Like other people wanting to kill you in return.<br /> <br /> Beasts are also one of the splats least likely to draw a meaningful distinction between what is and isn't human. Satiety doesn't care at all if a victim is a normal human, or a monster, as long as the Beast can generate shock in a fashion that satisfies their hunger at a high enough level for their current Satiety rating. Beasts are however prone to being clannish and feeding on family is worse for them (any they can form mechanically significant bonds of family to the majority of supernatural beings in the setting).<br /> -----------------<br /> <br /> I also notice Changeling isn't on the list? Not that CtL is difficult to place here.<br /> <br /> ------------------<br /> <br /> I'm also not sure how you want to codify things here. Just codify how &quot;human&quot; something needs to be to count for splats where human-ness matters? Or something broader?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-05T15:36:03-07:00","id":1480215,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1480164-multi-splat-when-do-you-ignore-breaking-points-for-killing-non-humans?p=1480196#post1480196\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Beasts are also one of the splats least likely to draw a meaningful distinction between what is and isn't human.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fer reals. Beasts don't stress over killing humans or monsters, they stress over killing people and persons.<br /> <br /> As for the larger picture point, my answer is never. If I don't call or ask for it, that means something about the character doing it in question, not a decision to ignore it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 05-05-2022, 06:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-05T16:32:04-07:00","id":1480217,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DontEatRawHagis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1480164-multi-splat-when-do-you-ignore-breaking-points-for-killing-non-humans#post1480164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Promethean = Torment (?) (Not a stat, but I'd say murder is probably a Torment Trigger though not RAW as far as I can tell)</div> </div> </div> </div>Specifically killing or injuring people or causing these things to happen through supernatural means (including superhuman traits) are steps backwards on the Pilgrimage, but normal murder doesn't interfere with the Created's ability to learn.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Geist/Sin-Eater = Crisis Point (?) (Not sure, Sin-Eaters seem very unphased to killing people unless its similar to their own or their Geist's death) </div> </div> </div>Sin-Eaters' personalized crisis point triggers can theoretically include circumstances where they commit murder, but most of the examples concern things happening to the character instead of things the character does themselves.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Mummy = Memory (?) (Probably not) </div> </div> </div>Pursuing a Judge's order solely to retain Sekhem or abandoning the meret to pursue a Judge's agenda can easily entail murder, given the vision of &quot;justice&quot; the Judges advocate. <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Deviant = Stability (?) (Talks about how Instability risks harming innocent people so seems like a contender) </div> </div> </div>Stability takes a ding when you fail to pursue the drives of your Conviction and/or Loyalty, and being the cause of a Loyalty Touchstone's destruction results in a worse-than-usual Instability than if they just died normally.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-07T00:33:03-07:00","id":1480352,"title":"","content":"Never. Murder of a sentient being is always relevant.<br /> <br /> It may have distinct impacts depending on the specific consequences the splat suffers and the perception of the character, but as a rule of thumb there's no inherent distinction between Human and Monster for such aspect of the game.<br /> <br /> You may factor circumstances in different ways, though. How much does perception factors in? A human killing a thing they suspect to be sentient should face a BP, but may have an easier time than usual if this suspicion has little to back it up and the thing didn't looked human. Killing something they know to not be sentient or human, but looks to much like the part should also trigger a BP, now without much help. Killing a sentient being they refuse to recognize as human may or may not be easier or harder, it depends. Knowledge and belief is a factor for Integrity, but it can't shake-off the shock entirely.<br /> <br /> That's the gist of it, but distinct consequence systems may factor things like perception and knowledge differently. If you can't figure out what that system means for you and how to use it, though, just not making a distinction between human and non-human is the best rule of thumb to not lose the themes and mood of the setting. If you thing killing humans shouldn't be inconsequential in your game, then killing supernaturals shouldn't either, this is where the psychological examination lies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}